.TH CSTRING_RFIND 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_rfind \- find the last occurrence of a substring
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

size_t cstring_rfind(cstr s, const char *needle);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Searches the string for the last occurrence of needle and returns its
zero-based starting index.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        String to search
needle   Substring to find (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Zero-based index of the last occurrence
ccol_invalid_size ((size_t)-1) if needle is not found
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_find (3)
